// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | CURRENT_DECISIONS: ADR-039 dashboard-derived-state-endpoint (2026-03-02)

#what_changed
=device-state.controller.ts: added getDerivedState() handler
  → calls deviceDerivedStateService.getLatest(deviceId)
  → throws NotFoundError if null
  → returns { deviceId, derived, lastSeen, stale, staledAt }
=device-state.routes.ts: registered GET /devices/:deviceId/derived-state
  → placed before /states/* routes (Fastify ordering)
  → preHandler: requireAuth + requirePermission('device-state:read')
  → Swagger schema with derived, lastSeen, stale, staledAt
=useDeviceData.ts (useDeviceRealtime): queryFn switched from /states/latest → /derived-state
  → response parsed as { deviceId, derived, lastSeen, stale, staledAt }
  → DeviceState cache object: { id:`derived-${deviceId}`, data:derived, derived, timestamp:lastSeen }
  → staleMeta seeded from queryFn response (latestState.stale/staledAt) — removed device.derivedStateMeta path

#tech_implications
~device_states (time-series) is now history/charts/exports ONLY — never for live display
~device_derived_states is canonical live snapshot for all dashboard gauge reads
~useDeviceRealtime callers: state.data contains derived fields only (no raw sensor fields on initial load)
  raw sensor fields still merged in on every WebSocket device:state event — no regression
~useDeviceFields unchanged: reads device.derivedState from GET /devices/:deviceId
~RealTimeGaugeBlock unchanged: reads latestState.derived?.[field] ?? latestState.data?.[field] — compatible
~/states/latest endpoint remains (not removed) — used by audit/raw data views

#constraints
!rule: dashboard MUST use /derived-state for live snapshot (ADR-039)
!rule: /states/latest is for historical/audit use only
~if device has no derived state (no workflow run yet) → 404 from /derived-state → gauge shows fallback value
~stale flag propagated from API response on hard refresh (no WebSocket needed for stale detection)
